A||N||25||87ECO5||"PONTIAC" Emblem on Rear of Car||||8||
Z||000000||87ECO5||06-01-2000||04:16 PM||||Can someone please tell me how Pontiac managed to improve everything about the car through its five year life <B><I>EXCEPT</I></B> for the "PONTIAC" emblem on the tail!?<P>The coupes (not sure about the fastbacks) had the very modern-looking "P O N T I A C" letters grooved into the plastic for '84 through '86 (just like the left headlight cover).  Then, when they got the new front and rear fascias in '87, the idiots at Pontiac decided a 70's-looking stick-on emblem would be better!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   Give me a fricking break!  And it's really not even a stick-on emblem.  The fascia has two holes that the emblem sticks into!  CAN ANYONE SAY - <B>DUH!!!!!</B><P>Anyway, I'm looking to replace this eyesore of an emblem with something nicer.  My idea (since I don't want to fill the holes and repaint the rear fascia) is to find a "PONTIAC" decal that's big enough to cover the area where this current emblem resides.<P>Anyone have any ideas?||||reg||8
Z||000001||tgowens||06-01-2000||04:59 PM||||why not just put a left headlight on the rear of the car???<P>Seriously, for a little investment you could have the grooved Pontiac cut from a left headlight door and use that on the rear of the car - the "Pontiac" could then be painted the same color as the car or in a contrasting color.......use it as a "stick-on" type of medallion with double face tape or even have a body shop cut out a matching section of the decklid and install the "Pontiac" in place, then refinish as desired.........<P>Just a thought..........||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||06-01-2000||07:53 PM||||I always wanted to pull a Formula badge off a new firebird formula and stick it there.  Its a cursive chrome thing!<P>I would recommend looking at Grand am, Grand prix, firebird, sunfire, bonniville, etc... new car pontiac badges before I cut badges off of my headlights. IMHO....<P>btw... You could get a nice vinyl sticker that says pontiac and it would look cool too||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||06-01-2000||08:02 PM||||<B>Formula</B> - a vinyl "PONTIAC" sticker is exactly what I was thinking.  I mean, they put a "Fiero" sticker on the decklid.  Why not the same thing for the brand name!?<P>Of course, I'd prefer the grooved letters like <B>tgowens</B> mentioned (and the earlier models had) but I'm not interested in the work required by that idea right now.<P>Now, where would I find one of these vinyl stickers?||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||06-01-2000||08:03 PM||||geeeeeeezzzzzzzzz Formula, I didn't mean to cut up the headlight door!!......I meant to get one from the bone yard and make an emblem from that. The headlight door is the only place I have seen the engraved 'Pontiac'..... your idea is good too -- there is no reason why an emblem of any kind can't be put on the back -- ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||06-01-2000||08:06 PM||||E-mail me and I can get you one made, I'm pretty sure bcm still has some "Fiero" grey in stock.  If its not to expensive I'll pay for everything. I plan on getting one made for my car too so if its under $10 for both I'll just send you one. send dimensions too!||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||06-01-2000||08:09 PM||||hmmmmmm, ya got me thinkin now.......next time I go up to the Fiero Shop maybe I can get a headlight door, use a sabre saw to cut out the 'Pontiac', then run a router around the edges to finish it and then apply it to the decklid with double-stick tape -- might look kinda cool -- don't know tho, I have an '87 GT and there is no place to put it!! But, i might just try making one anyway.......87ECO5, what color is your car? maybe I'll make you one and send it to you and if you like it I might just go into the emblem business!! (it would supplement my web design business nicely, doncha think??).....hmmmmm, nice way to make club emblems too (he says, thinking out loud... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||06-01-2000||08:15 PM||||Holy cow, guys!  This is just another example of how great this forum is!<P><B>Formula</B> - I'll send you an email in a little bit about dimensions.  FieroWife has the car right now so I can't get measurements.  But, I think the emblem is about 9" long and 2" high.  Again, I'll get an email to you soon.<P><B>tgowens</B> - My coupe is white.<P>Thanks, guys!  Long live PFF!!!!!||||reg||14
